    "title": "Where to watch Nebraska-Iowa Sweet 16 basketball: Time, TV channel",
    "text": "March 26, 2026, 4:09 a.m. CTThe Nebraska Cornhuskers will face the Iowa Hawkeyes on Thursday in the Sweet 16 of the NCAA Tournament. This is the Huskers' first Sweet 16 in program history, while Iowa is playing in its first Sweet 16 since 1999.Nebraska defeated Vanderbilt 74-72 in the second round of the NCAA Tournament. Iowa advanced after beating the defending national champion, the Florida Gators, 73-72.This will be the third time these two teams have played this season. Nebraska lost at Iowa, 57-52, back on Feb. 17. Bennett Stirtz played all 40 minutes and led the Hawkeyes with 25 points. Pryce Sandfort led the Huskers with only 13 points in 37 minutes.The Huskers returned the favor in Lincoln on March 8, defeating the Hawkeyes 84-75 in overtime. Sam Hoiberg and Pryce Sandfort led Nebraska in scoring with 15 points each. Iowa's Kael Combs and Cooper Koch each had 18 points in the defeat.Nebraska-Iowa play in the Sweet 16 of the NCAA Tournament on Thursday, March 26 at 6:30 p.m. CT on TBS. The winner will play the winner of the Sweet 16 game between Illinois and Houston.Watch Nebraska-Iowa in the Sweet 16 on SlingHere's how to watch the Nebraska-Iowa game Thursday, including time, TV schedule, and streaming information:What channel is the Nebraska-Iowa basketball game on?TV Channel: TBSLivestream: SlingNebraska-Iowa can be seen on TBS in the Sweet 16 of the 2026 NCAA Tournament. Kevin Harlan, Robbie Hummel, Stan Van Gundy and Lauren Shehadi will call the game from the Toyota Center. Streaming options for the game include Sling.Nebraska-Iowa basketball start time for ThursdayDate: Thursday, March 26Start time: 6:30 p.m. CTThe Nebraska-Iowa basketball game starts at 6:30 p.m. CT from the Toyota Center in Houston, TX.Nebraska-Iowa oddsOdds courtesy of BetMGM as of Thursday, March 26Money: Nebraska (-130)/Iowa (+110)ODDS: Nebraska -1.5 (-110)O/U: 131 1/2 (-110)We occasionally recommend interesting products and services. If you make a purchase by clicking one of the links, we may earn an affiliate fee. USA TODAY Network newsrooms operate independently, and this doesn't influence our coverage.Contact/Follow us @CornhuskersWire on X (formerly Twitter) and like our page on Facebook to follow ongoing coverage of Nebraska news, notes and opinions.",
